<</Type /StructElem
/P 157 0 R
/S /P
/E (Since becoming Indonesias Minister of Health in 2020, Minister Budi has drawn on his experience across health and finance to make sustainable financing an integral part of the countrys health transformation. Working across government and with development partners, he has translated national health priorities into investment needs and mobilised resources to accelerate transformation at scale.)
/K [10]
/Pg 18 0 R
>>
endobj
340 0 obj
<</Type /StructElem
/P 157 0 R
/S /P
/E (This approach has helped mobilise US$8.75 billion in external financing, comprising US$3.75 billion in grants and US$5 billion from multilateral development banks. Of the MDB financing, US$4 billion supports a government-led Health Systems Strengthening programme co-financed by the World Bank, ADB, AIIB and IsDB„the World Banks largest-ever health-sector investment and the largest MDB co-investment in human development. The investment is equipping over 10,000 primary healthcare facilities, 500 public-health laboratories and 600 hospitals with medical equipment, with a particular focus on strengthening cancer, cardiac, stroke and uro-nephrology services.)
/K [11]
/Pg 18 0 R
>>
endobj
